Kubernetes Secrets Enumeration and Manipulation via API Server

This threat hunting scenario detects potentially suspicious access to Kubernetes Secrets through the Kubernetes API server, including list, get, create, update, and delete operations. Kubernetes Secrets may contain sensitive information such as application credentials, API keys, tokens, certificates, and other authentication material. From a threat-hunting perspective, unexpected enumeration or modification of Secrets can indicate an adversary attempting to discover credentials, obtain application access, or manipulate the cluster's management plane.

The hunt should focus on the identity performing the operation, requested resource, authorization result, source IP, and geographic/ASN information. Particular attention should be given to bulk Secret enumeration, access from unusual source addresses, unexpected service accounts or users, and destructive or modification operations. Correlating Secret access with Kubernetes authentication events, API activity, workload changes, and subsequent use of discovered credentials can help determine whether the behavior represents legitimate administrative activity or potential compromise.

MITRE ATT&CK Mapping:

T1552.007 – Unsecured Credentials: Container API
T1528 – Steal Application Access Token
T1613 – Container Service

Cortex:
// Kubernetes Secrets Enumeration via API Server (Management Plane)
// Detects listing, reading, and creation of secrets via the K8s API

dataset = cloud_audit_logs
| filter resource_type_orig = "k8s.io"
| filter operation_name_orig in ("io.k8s.core.v1.secrets.list", "io.k8s.core.v1.secrets.get", "io.k8s.core.v1.secrets.create", "io.k8s.core.v1.secrets.update", "io.k8s.core.v1.secrets.delete")
| alter principal = json_extract_scalar(raw_log, "$.protoPayload.authenticationInfo.principalEmail")
| alter auth_granted = json_extract_scalar(raw_log, "$.protoPayload.authorizationInfo[0].granted")
| alter auth_resource = json_extract_scalar(raw_log, "$.protoPayload.authorizationInfo[0].resource")
| alter op_risk = if(
    operation_name_orig contains "list", "ENUM",
    operation_name_orig contains "delete", "DESTROY",
    operation_name_orig contains "create", "CREATE",
    operation_name_orig contains "update", "MODIFY",
    "READ"
)
//| filter principal ~= ""
//| filter op_risk = "ENUM"
| fields _time, principal, operation_name_orig, op_risk, auth_granted, auth_resource, referenced_resource_name, caller_ip, caller_ip_geolocation, caller_ip_asn_org
